  "prompt": "Fix: the organize permission must also cover units, tools, labels, recipe actions and the seeders.\n\nThe \"User can organize group data\" flag (can_organize) gates foods, tags and categories, declared on their routes with require(Perm.GROUP_ORGANIZE). Units, tools, multi-purpose labels, household recipe actions and the food/unit seeders are still open to every member, although the documentation describes the permission as covering organizers in general.\n\nExpected:\n- These routes declare Perm.GROUP_ORGANIZE through the route-permission dependency, so a user without can_organize gets 403 before the body is read or validated, and a user with it is not refused (any status other than 403, since the check runs first): POST /api/units, PUT /api/units/merge, PUT /api/units/{item_id}, DELETE /api/units/{item_id}; POST /api/organizers/tools, PUT /api/organizers/tools/{item_id}, DELETE /api/organizers/tools/{item_id}; POST /api/groups/labels, PUT /api/groups/labels/{item_id}, DELETE /api/groups/labels/{item_id}; POST /api/households/recipe-actions, PUT /api/households/recipe-actions/{item_id}, DELETE /api/households/recipe-actions/{item_id}; POST /api/groups/seeders/foods, POST /api/groups/seeders/units.\n- The table of declared permissions read back from app.routes grows by exactly these entries under GROUP_ORGANIZE; no other route changes its declared permission.\n- Reads (the lists, single items, /empty) stay open to every member.\n- Docs: the permissions page and the frontend wording for the permission say it covers foods, units, tools, labels, tags, categories and recipe actions; a frontend announcement about the change is welcome (none of this is graded).\n\nTests: `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/integration_tests/test_route_permissions.py tests/integration_tests/category_tag_tool_tests` for quick loops; the whole backend suite is `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests` (about 8 minutes).",
  "title": "fix: require can_organize to manage units, tools, labels, recipe actions (#8783)",
